    "title": "Cade Cunningham granted NBA awards eligibility despite injury – 910News.com",
    "text": "Skip to MainSkip to MainSportsCade Cunningham granted NBA awards eligibility despite injury Jake Boss04-16-2026 at 03:27:09 PM EDTLink Copied!Cade Cunningham, Kevin Durant (AP News / Duane Burleson) - Detroit Pistons guard Cade Cunningham (2) goes to the basket against Phoenix Suns forward Kevin Durant (35) during the first half of a preseason NBA basketball game Sunday, Oct. 8, 2023, in Detroit. (AP Photo/Duane Burleson)DETROIT - The NBA and NBA Players Association granted Cade Cunningham NBA awards eligibility on Thursday under the ‘extraordinary circumstances’ clause.Cunningham finished the regular season having played in 64 games, falling one short of the league’s 65-game minimum due to the collapsed lung he suffered towards the end of the regular season.The former first-overall pick was playing at an MVP caliber prior to his injury, and returned for the final three games of the season to add to his case.AdvertisementCunningham finished the regular season averaging 23.9 points and 9.9 assists per game in Detroit’s best season in two decades.NBA awards ballots will be sent to voters Thursday, and results will be revealed as the playoffs unfold. Top VideosIn this article:Digital ExclusiveLink Copied!Local Trending News MoreSettingsFull Screen (F)Play (SPACE)Read More (Shift + O) Quality Auto ConnatixV323954724 Quality 360p 720p HD 1080p HD Auto(360p) 00:0003:06 360p 720p HD 1080p HD Auto(360p) ConnatixV323954724 Read More 1/100:19910MediaGroup - RSS Feed Skip Ad Continue watchingTragic murder-suicide leaves three deceased in Stanwood homeafter the adVisit Advertiser websiteGO TO PAGEPopular SPORTSTitans hand Petoskey first loss, maintain top conference spotSPORTSSt. Francis baseball team’s 4-0 start ends with 6-5 loss to Elk Rapids SPORTSSacred Heart baseball team cruises to 12-0 startFish & Game ReportApr 22Apr 23Apr 24PredictionAverageMajor Times5:26 AM - 7:26 AM5:56 PM - 7:56 PMMinor Times1:48 AM - 2:48 AM1:48 AM - 2:48 AMFull Report Advertisement*